{title: Life in Abundance}
{subtitle: John 10:7–11}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
My [Bb]granddad kept a flock of sheep [Eb]out past the county line [Bb]
He knew them every one by name and they [F]all knew his sign
[Eb]He'd sleep across the gateway when the [Bb]coyotes came a[Gm]round
[Eb]And not a lamb was taken while he [F]lay upon the ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]I came that they may have [Bb/D][Eb]life
And have it in a[Bb]bundance
[F]I am the good [Gm]shepherd
The [Eb]good shepherd lays [F]down his life for the [Bb]sheep
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]I am the gate
Whoever [Eb]enters through me [Bb]will be saved
He will come in and go out [F]and find pasture
[Eb]The thief comes only to steal [Bb]and kill [F/A]and de[Gm]stroy
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Gm] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [F] |
| [F] |

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]I came that they may have [Bb/D][Eb]life
And have it in abun[Bb]dance
[F]I am the good [Gm]shepherd
[Gm7/F]The [Eb]good shepherd lays [F]down his life for the [Bb]sheep
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
I've [Gm]wandered from the [F/A]gateway and [Bb]I've heard the stranger [Eb]call
But [Gm]I know my shep[F/A]herd's voice now [Eb]and I know he gave it all
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]I came that they may have [Eb]life
And have it in abun[Bb]dance
{end_of_verse}

